{"id":"7df291a6731ae8a3","group":"58","path":"58/batch01/58-df-integrability.md","title":"Integrability","display":"df-integrability — Integrability","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-integrability","aliases":["58-df-integrability","Integrability"],"display":"df-integrability — Integrability","depends_on":["[[../batch02/58-df-integral.md]]","[[../batch12/58-df-measure-space.md]]","[[../batch07/58-df-measurable-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-integrability"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-integrability</span><span>Integrability</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-integrability — Integrability"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"4884f45058a56aac\" href=\"?note=4884f45058a56aac\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-integral.md\">../batch02/58-df-integral.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"83a15c7e9b3817dc\" href=\"?note=83a15c7e9b3817dc\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-measure-space.md\">../batch12/58-df-measure-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"bbbec05fde1d3b01\" href=\"?note=bbbec05fde1d3b01\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-measurable-function.md\">../batch07/58-df-measurable-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X,\\mathcal F,\\mu,f,p\\in V\">\\(X,\\mathcal F,\\mu,f,p\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S\\)</span> (measure-space predicate; see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"83a15c7e9b3817dc\" href=\"?note=83a15c7e9b3817dc\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-measure-space.md\">../batch12/58-df-measure-space.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure3RealMeasurableFunction}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure3RealMeasurableFunction}_S\\)</span> (real measurable-function predicate; see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"bbbec05fde1d3b01\" href=\"?note=bbbec05fde1d3b01\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-measurable-function.md\">../batch07/58-df-measurable-function.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal B_+\">\\(\\mathcal B_+\\)</span> (the Borel sigma-algebra on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"[0,\\infty]\">\\([0,\\infty]\\)</span> used by the integral dependency)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Measurable}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Measurable}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\int_Xg\\,d\\mu\">\\(\\int_Xg\\,d\\mu\\)</span> (measurability and nonnegative Lebesgue integral from the dependencies)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PIntegrable}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{PIntegrable}_S\\)</span> (<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p\">\\(p\\)</span>-integrability predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}integrability}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{PIntegrable}_S(f,p,X,\\mathcal F,\\mu)\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(X,\\mathcal F,\\mu)\n\\land\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure3RealMeasurableFunction}_S(X,\\mathcal F,f)\n\\land p\\in\\mathbb R\\land1\\leq p&lt;\\infty\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\exists g\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\ng\\in[0,\\infty]^X\n\\land\\forall x\\in X\\;(g(x)=|f(x)|^p)\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{23mm}{}\\land\n\\mathrm{Measurable}_S(g;(X,\\mathcal F),([0,\\infty],\\mathcal B_+))\n\\land\\int_Xg\\,d\\mu&lt;\\infty\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}integrability}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{PIntegrable}_S(f,p,X,\\mathcal F,\\mu)\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(X,\\mathcal F,\\mu)\n\\land\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure3RealMeasurableFunction}_S(X,\\mathcal F,f)\n\\land p\\in\\mathbb R\\land1\\leq p&lt;\\infty\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\exists g\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\ng\\in[0,\\infty]^X\n\\land\\forall x\\in X\\;(g(x)=|f(x)|^p)\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{23mm}{}\\land\n\\mathrm{Measurable}_S(g;(X,\\mathcal F),([0,\\infty],\\mathcal B_+))\n\\land\\int_Xg\\,d\\mu&lt;\\infty\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p=1\">\\(p=1\\)</span> recovers ordinary absolute integrability.</li>\n<li>The nonnegative integrand is now a bound set function whose measurability is checked before applying the integral interface.</li>\n<li>The <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L^p\">\\(L^p\\)</span> space is obtained by quotienting <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p\">\\(p\\)</span>-integrable measurable functions by equality almost everywhere.</li>\n<li>Essential boundedness (<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p=\\infty\">\\(p=\\infty\\)</span>) is a separate definition.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L^q \\subseteq L^p\">\\(L^q \\subseteq L^p\\)</span> for <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"q &gt; p\">\\(q &gt; p\\)</span> when <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu(X) &lt; \\infty\">\\(\\mu(X) &lt; \\infty\\)</span></li>\n<li>Minkowski: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\|f+g\\|_p \\leq \\|f\\|_p + \\|g\\|_p\">\\(\\|f+g\\|_p \\leq \\|f\\|_p + \\|g\\|_p\\)</span></li>\n<li>Inclusions: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L^1 \\supseteq L^2 \\supseteq L^3 \\supseteq \\ldots\">\\(L^1 \\supseteq L^2 \\supseteq L^3 \\supseteq \\ldots\\)</span> for probability spaces</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Rudin, Real and Complex Analysis</li>\n<li>Folland, Real Analysis</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch02/58-df-integral.md","status":"resolved","id":"4884f45058a56aac","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-df-integral.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch12/58-df-measure-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"83a15c7e9b3817dc","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-measure-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch07/58-df-measurable-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"bbbec05fde1d3b01","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch07/58-df-measurable-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch12/58-df-measure-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"83a15c7e9b3817dc","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S$ (measure-space predicate; see [[../batch12/58-df-measure-space.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch07/58-df-measurable-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"bbbec05fde1d3b01","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure3RealMeasurableFunction}_S$ (real measurable-function predicate; see [[../batch07/58-df-measurable-function.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"X,\\mathcal F,\\mu,f,p\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure3RealMeasurableFunction}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal B_+","display":false},{"tex":"[0,\\infty]","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Measurable}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\int_Xg\\,d\\mu","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{PIntegrable}_S","display":false},{"tex":"p","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}integrability}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{PIntegrable}_S(f,p,X,\\mathcal F,\\mu)\n\\leftrightarrow{}&\n\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(X,\\mathcal F,\\mu)\n\\land\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure3RealMeasurableFunction}_S(X,\\mathcal F,f)\n\\land p\\in\\mathbb R\\land1\\leq p<\\infty\\\\\n&{}\\land\\exists g\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\ng\\in[0,\\infty]^X\n\\land\\forall x\\in X\\;(g(x)=|f(x)|^p)\\\\\n&\\hspace{23mm}{}\\land\n\\mathrm{Measurable}_S(g;(X,\\mathcal F),([0,\\infty],\\mathcal B_+))\n\\land\\int_Xg\\,d\\mu<\\infty\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"p=1","display":false},{"tex":"L^p","display":false},{"tex":"p","display":false},{"tex":"p=\\infty","display":false},{"tex":"L^q \\subseteq L^p","display":false},{"tex":"q > p","display":false},{"tex":"\\mu(X) < \\infty","display":false},{"tex":"\\|f+g\\|_p \\leq \\|f\\|_p + \\|g\\|_p","display":false},{"tex":"L^1 \\supseteq L^2 \\supseteq L^3 \\supseteq \\ldots","display":false}],"bytes":2072,"backlinks":[{"id":"cebc92aa41f3a49c","anchor":"ref-5","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"外部接口 $\\mathrm{PIntegrable}$ 取 [[../batch01/58-df-integrability.md]] 的同名定义与参数次序。"},{"id":"cce18fac72649ea9","anchor":"ref-7","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{PIntegrable}_S(f,1,X,\\Sigma,\\mu)$ (integrable measurable function, see [[../batch01/58-df-integrability]])"},{"id":"8ee39070d2fffa3c","anchor":"ref-7","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{PIntegrable}_S$ (integrability predicate, see [[../batch01/58-df-integrability]])"},{"id":"8160ac3d14bcbf65","anchor":"ref-5","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"34f1c7d95297d4b7","anchor":"ref-7","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{PIntegrable}_S\\subseteq V^5$ (see [[../batch01/58-df-integrability.md]])."},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-694","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch01/58-df-integrability.md|58-df-integrability]]（batch01）"}],"